{"name":"Cloistered Garden","hex":"#99b090","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cloistered","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dwelling or raised in, or as if in, cloisters; solitary.","Isolated, protected, hidden away for the sake of maintaining innocence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of cloister"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloistered"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloister","blocks":[{"text":"A cloister is a covered walk, open gallery, or open arcade running along the walls of buildings and forming a quadrangle or garth. The attachment of a cloister to a cathedral or church, commonly against a warm southern flank, usually indicates that it is part of a monastic foundation, \"forming a continuous and solid architectural barrier... that effectively separates the world of the monks from that of the serfs and workmen, whose lives and works went forward outside and around the cloister.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloister%2C_Lutheran_Church_of_the_Redeemer_%28Jerusalem%29_%2817%29.jpg/330px-Cloister%2C_Lutheran_Church_of_the_Redeemer_%28Jerusalem%29_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloister","wikidata":"Q1430154"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment o